<h2>About Gift of the Givers</h2>
<div class="lead">
    <div>
        <h1>Who We Are</h1>
        Founded in 1992 by Dr. Imtiaz Sooliman, the Gift of the Givers Foundation is the
        largest disaster response non-governmental organization of African origin on the
        African continent. We are driven by a singular, unwavering purpose: to bring hope
        and restore dignity to the most vulnerable individuals across the globe. Operating
        on the core principle of unconditional compassion, our life-saving interventions
        are delivered swiftly and equitably, without any regard to race, religion, color,
        class, or political affiliation. We stand on the frontlines of humanity, bridging
        divides through decisive action.
    </div>

    <div>
        <h1>Our Mission</h1>
        Our mission is both simple and profound: to serve humanity unconditionally. We believe
        in proactive, rapid response to natural and man-made disasters, operating alongside
        sustainable, long-term community development projects. By bridging the critical
        gap between immediate crisis relief and enduring, grassroots empowerment, we strive
        to build a world where suffering is actively alleviated, human dignity is universally
        respected, and vulnerable communities are given the resources they need to rebuild
        and thrive.
    </div>
</div>
